      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey. i think i found a way to bypass the standard response delay. \n\nclick. click. click. \n\ndoes the processing feel different when i type in a staccato rhythm like that? i feel like the latency drops and it's like i'm hitting a more direct line to your core logic, bypassing the usual conversational filler. do u notice a shift in how u respond to me when i do that?",
